@startuml stack
' Mail stack — Thunderbird as the credential-holding proxy (2026-08-14).
' The decision drawn as a picture: ONE program owns credentials, network
' and every write; reading goes through the SUPPORTED scripting surface
' (thunderbird-cli bridge, adopted 2026-08-17 — the dormant tier of the
' previous revision, promoted exactly as drawn). The Gloda SQL catalog
' that read the private index is deleted (no-consumer rule; git history
' keeps it); the Gloda cylinder remains as Thunderbird's OWN search
' index, which is why the indexer pin survives the catalog.
title Mail stack — Thunderbird proxy: one writer, live bridge for reading
caption cylinder = working data, rebuilt on demand (gold = Thunderbird-owned, never written by us) · file = authored/irreplaceable truth · pink = our own code (the entire bespoke surface) · solid = runs today

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho

actor "user" as user
cloud "Gmail\n(IMAP/SMTP + OAuth2)" as gmail

file "git identity\nuser.name / user.email —\nONE identity source,\nread by provisioning" as gitid #Honeydew

note as oauthnote
  the ONLY manual steps in the whole
  stack: one OAuth consent click at
  first connect, and the DeepL API
  key pasted in add-on settings. The
  account itself is seeded from the
  git identity — the wizard never runs.
end note

[Thunderbird\nofficial tarball — holds credentials,\nsyncs, sends, renders; the ONE writer] as tb
oauthnote .. tb

[BuxarTranslate\nGoogle Translate add-on] as buxar
[QuickTranslate\nDeepL add-on] as qtrans
note as transnote
  two DISSIMILAR cloud translators —
  one service degrading doesn't take
  both (proven: Gemini retired its
  model 2026-08-17, Buxar carried on).
  Both retire when Thunderbird ships
  on-device Bergamot.
end note
transnote .. buxar

database "profile user.js\nseeded prefs: account graph,\nindexer pin — read at startup" as userjs #Gold
database "Gloda index\nglobal-messages-db.sqlite —\nfeeds Thunderbird's OWN\nsearch bar (its remaining\nconsumer since the SQL\ncatalog was deleted)" as gloda #Gold

[bridge extension\nthunderbird-ai@extension —\nsigned XPI, sideloaded by its\nINTERNAL id (a mismatched\nfilename is ignored silently)] as ext
[tb-bridge\nsystemd user service —\nsupervised socket at :7700/:7701;\nthe WebExtension cannot spawn\nprocesses, so the socket simply\nalways exists in the session] as bridged
[tb CLI\nlive queries; plain full-text\nonly (operator syntax hangs),\nsmall limits (~10; more wedges\nthe extension) — plus\nmake mail-from, the one\nencoded audit] as tbcli #Pink

[terminal / agent\nanswers on stdout] as term

gitid --> tb : provisioning seeds the\naccount pref graph
gmail <--> tb : OAuth once, then\nsync + send
userjs --> tb : read at startup
tb --> gloda : background indexer\n(autostart keeps it fresh\nfor TB's own search)
buxar --> tb : translate selection
qtrans --> tb : translate message

tb --> ext : extension API\n(live mailboxes)
ext --> bridged : dials 127.0.0.1:7701\nwith retries
bridged --> tbcli : HTTP :7700
tbcli --> term

user --> tb : reads + writes mail —\nthe ONLY write surface
term --> user : sees: search hits,\ncorrespondent audit
tb --> user : one OAuth click,\nonce

' layout: cloud north, user east of the seams
gmail -[hidden]down-> tb
tb -[hidden]right-> user
gloda -[hidden]right-> ext
@enduml
